{
  "documents": [
    "Proyecto de investigación (replanteado) (2).pdf - Archivo --- Página 1 ---\nPhysics\nBenjamín Sánchez Arenas\nElectroplating\n¿What is the relation between voltage and speed\nof electroplating while maintaining a constant\nwatt measurement?",
    "Dante Caleb Cardoso Antonio\nA01772445\n--- Página 2 ---\nMy intention is to make an experiment to measure the relation of the electricity and\nthe time it takes to get to a certain thickness of metal using electroplating, so I want to\nend with a formula or relation for this process. I chose this topic because I am kind of\nfamiliarized with it, at first it was the impression on how personalized shapes could be\ncovered on a metal, this can add them many characteristics, but in plastics, it is most\ncommonly used for esthetic purposes, for example, making keychains, accessories or\nornaments, so I think this technique has a lot of potential especially on the mechanical\nside, like adding a little bit of resistance or stopping plastic parts from wearing, I like\ncombining this with 3d printing one of my favorite hobbies, but after trying it I\nnoticed there are many variables that need to be covered to achieve a good\nelectroplating one of them being electricity, so this is why I chose this topic for my\ninternal assessment, I want to have a good idea of how voltage influence in the speed\nand quality of the final result\nElectroplating is a process where ions of a metal, normally copper.",
    "Are placed on the\ncathode and stack together to form a thick layer of metal, in industrial areas, it is used\nto cover pieces in niquel to give it resistance, shine or certain properties depending on\nthe metal, the process involves electricity to dissolve the copper in copper ions and\nelectrons, that travel in the electrolytic bath and then on the cathode they combine the\nelectrons with copper ions and form copper on the surface, cooper electroplating can\nhave many variables, temperature, resistance of the anode, voltage, current, quality of\nthe electricity, and many others that influence the quality, thickness, surface and time,\nbut on this experiment I will be focusing on one dependant and an independent\nvariable, the dependant being the thickness of the layer formed on the cube, and the\nindependent variable being the input electricity, in this case I will maintain the watts\nalways the same, but the voltage and current will be modulated. The electroplated objects will be 10 3d printed blocks with small hooks to tie them\nwith cable, they will have the same surface area (0.1m2), to make sure we can make a\ngood approach of how electricity affects the thickness of the metal overtime, the\n--- Página 3 ---\nmaterial has to conduct electricity, so I will add painting that conducts electricity using\ngraphite, and measure the resistance so I can add that factor to the formula.",
    "There were 10 plastic pieces in total, which were covered in electric paint, they had an\nimpedance of approximately 10 ohms/ cm, then started the electroplating process\n--- Página 4 ---\nResults\nThe first time was 22 minutes to get fully covered, while the second was 16 minutes, we can\nsee the quality is also better,\nThe first voltage was 1 and 0.5 amps while the second 0.250 amps and 2 v, getting 1 watt\ntotal for both, the third 0.33 amp and 3 v, the fourth 0.25 amp and 4V, while the fifth is 0.2\namp and 5 v\nWe can identify a negative relation with the voltage and time needed to electroplate,\nbecause when more voltage is added, less time is needed regardless of the intensity."
  ],
